## When generating tests

For every new workflow, generate:
1. A **validator test** that runs the workflow definition through WorkflowValidator
2. A **happy path integration test** that mocks API_CALL responses and asserts the
   final DB_OPERATION was called with the correct data
3. A **guard clause test per RULE_CHECK** that verifies STOP_EXIT halts execution
4. An **HTTP route test** that sends a request and asserts the response status/body

## Checklist before completing any workflow task

- [ ] All business logic is in workflow steps, not custom code
- [ ] Steps are ordered so storeAs outputs precede $.references
- [ ] Every RULE_CHECK has a matching entry in rules/registry.ts
- [ ] No duplicate step IDs
- [ ] DB_OPERATION data mappings use only simple $.references
- [ ] HTTP route maps all outcomes (COMPLETED, STOP_EXIT, FAIL_JOB, RUN_WORKFLOW)
- [ ] No Wait states — async follow-ups use webhooks or separate endpoints
- [ ] No Parallel branches — flattened or wrapped in batch service method
- [ ] Tests cover happy path + each guard clause + HTTP response codes
- [ ] WorkflowValidator.validateAllOrThrow() passes
